---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PulsePreview from '../components/PulsePreview.astro';
import PulseFeatureGrid from '../components/PulseFeatureGrid.astro';
import PulseWorkflow from '../components/PulseWorkflow.astro';
import '../styles/pulse.css';
---
<Base>
  <article class="pulse-page">
    <header class="pulse-shell pulse-reveal pulse-hero">
      <div class="pulse-reveal-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">IT KEEPERS PULSE · UNDER DEVELOPMENT</p>
        <h1>Your IT environment.<br />One clear view.</h1>
        <p>IT Keepers Pulse is under development as a client visibility platform for the systems ITKeepers manages — users, devices, security, Microsoft 365, licensing, reports and support activity.</p>
        <p>ITKeepers manages the environment. Pulse is designed to make that work visible.</p>
        <div class="pulse-actions"><a class="btn" href="#one-view">Explore planned views <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><a class="pulse-text-link" href="/contact/?type=review">Book a Free IT Consultation</a></div>
      </div>
      <PulsePreview />
    </header>
    <section class="pulse-shell pulse-capabilities" id="one-view" aria-labelledby="pulse-one-view">
      <div class="pulse-section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">ONE VIEW</p><h2 id="pulse-one-view">See what is happening across your IT environment.</h2><p>You should not need to interpret five different admin portals or wait until something fails to understand your IT. Pulse is designed to bring the important signals into a managed IT dashboard built around clarity.</p></div>
      <PulseFeatureGrid />
      <p class="pulse-capability-note">IT Keepers Pulse is under development. The preview uses sample data; planned views, data sources, reporting and support integrations depend on development and agreed service scope. Discuss development status with our team.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="pulse-shell" aria-labelledby="pulse-action-title">
      <div class="pulse-section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">VISIBLE ACCOUNTABILITY</p><h2 id="pulse-action-title">From monitoring to action.</h2><p>You should not have to discover an IT issue before your IT provider does. When ITKeepers detects something that requires attention, the team investigates it. Pulse is designed to connect the state of your environment with the work happening around it.</p><p>The planned view would bring status, ownership and follow-up together. Resolution remains the team's work, with handling determined by the issue and your agreed service scope. See <a class="disclosure-link" href="/how-we-work/">how engineers review and follow up on IT work</a>.</p></div>
      <PulseWorkflow />
    </section>
    <section class="pulse-shell pulse-ownership" aria-labelledby="pulse-ownership-title">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">MANAGED BY ITKEEPERS. VISIBLE TO YOU.</p><h2 id="pulse-ownership-title">Visibility without another platform to manage.</h2><p>IT Keepers Pulse is designed as a client-facing view of your managed IT environment, rather than another monitoring tool for your team to operate.</p><p>Your IT person is a team. Pulse is designed to show what that team is managing.</p><a class="pulse-text-link" href="/services/managed-it/">Explore Managed IT <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
    </section>
    <section class="pulse-shell pulse-closing" aria-labelledby="pulse-contact-title"><div class="pulse-section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">LET'S TALK ABOUT YOUR ENVIRONMENT</p><h2 id="pulse-contact-title">A clearer view starts with the right context.</h2><p>Tell us what you manage today and where visibility is missing. Our team can discuss Pulse development status and the views and integrations proposed for your environment.</p><a class="btn" href="/contact/?type=review">Book a Free IT Consultation <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></section>
  </article>
</Base>
